# B15 measurement inputs — deliberately NOT committed.
#
# `shortcuts.jsonl` and `apps.jsonl` are a dump of the owner's phone: every installed app's label and
# every shortcut its apps publish. That is an inventory of what a person has and uses, and the review
# of the idea corpus already named the class ("the installed-app list is sensitive — it profiles the
# user"). Committing it would put that inventory in git history permanently, where deleting it later
# does not remove it.
#
# `corpus.txt` is the owner's own phrasings — what they would actually ask their phone to do. Same
# argument, and additionally B15's methodology requires it be written blind, so it is an input to one
# measurement rather than a fixture the project maintains.
#
# What IS committed is the REPORT: counts per decline category, with no labels. See README.md for how
# to regenerate these three files.
shortcuts.jsonl
apps.jsonl
corpus.txt
